{"run_id": "piloto-2", "question_id": "A002-T1-02", "system": "rag", "ingest_step": 5, "answer": "The four discrete editing actions are ADD, UPDATE, DELETE, and NOOP [2602.06052#s45.p1]. ADD writes a new entry; UPDATE rewrites or merges an existing entry; DELETE removes an entry that is contradicted or outdated; and NOOP means no update is made because the information is already covered or not important for long-term memory [2602.06052#s45.p1].", "abstained": false, "citations": ["2602.06052#s45.p1"], "context_tokens": 1549, "input_tokens": 1498, "output_tokens": 87, "latency_s": 1.0908595689979848, "cost_usd": 0.000516168, "model": "deepseek-flash", "temperature": 0.0, "timestamp": "2026-11-10T02:14:35Z"}
